SUMMARY:What Are People For: Design Philosophy by Patrick Whitney
LOCATION:MIT\, 134 MASSACHUSETTS Avenue\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:What Are People For: Design Philosophy by Patrick Whitney Bosto
 n-Cambridge Premiere of Gary Hustwit’s New Film and Interactive Design W
 orkshop Join the Morningside Academy of Design for the Boston-Cambridge Pr
 emiere of What Are People For: Design Philosophy by Patrick Whitney\, the 
 latest short film by acclaimed design documentarian Gary Hutwit (Helvetica
 \, Objectified\, Urbanized\, Eno)\, and interactive design workshop on Oct
 ober 24th. Explore how design can address today's most complex challenges 
 from 2-5pm with a hands-on workshop led by Evan Chan and André Nogueira. 
 Chan and Nogueira will introduce the Whole View model\, a systems design a
 pproach for reframing problems\, surfacing the perspectives of diverse sta
 keholders\, and finding new pathways forward in situations where expertise
  is abundant but fragmented. The session is designed for cross-sector lead
 ers grappling with problems too complex for any one discipline to solve al
 one.\nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/event/what-are-people-for\nFrom Pushpin Bos
 ton: https://pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/what-are-people-for
END:VEVENT
